---
import { product } from "../product";
import { actionDetail, actionLabel, type Release } from "../release";
interface Props {
  release: Release | null;
}
const { release } = Astro.props;
const profiles = release?.config.profiles ?? [];
const gestures = [
  ["single", "TAP"],
  ["double", "DOUBLE TAP"],
  ["long", "HOLD"],
] as const;
---

<section class="guide-grid" aria-label="Macro field guide">
  <article class="panel guide-panel controls-panel">
    <div class="panel-heading">
      <h2>02 / KNOW YOUR CONTROLS</h2><span class="small-tag">DOSSIER</span>
    </div>
    <div class="controls-brief">
      <p class="body-copy">
        Two operative buttons, <strong>A / MAIN</strong> and <strong
          >B / SIDE</strong
        >, each read three gestures: <strong>TAP</strong>, <strong
          >DOUBLE TAP</strong
        >, and <strong>HOLD</strong>. That is six slots per profile. A slot
        fires a key combo, types a text string, or plays a sequence.
      </p>
      <ul class="picker-keys" aria-label="Profile picker controls">
        <li><kbd>A + B</kbd><span>Open the profile picker</span></li>
        <li><kbd>B</kbd><span>Next profile</span></li>
        <li><kbd>A</kbd><span>Select and engage</span></li>
        <li>
          <kbd>A + B</kbd><span>Cancel (or wait 10 s idle)</span>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <p class="micro-copy">
      The last engaged profile is remembered across reboots. A hold fires once
      and suppresses the tap on release. Any press aborts a macro in progress.
      The separate reset/power button is not a control.
    </p>
    {
      release && profiles.length > 0 ? (
        <div class="profile-list">
          {profiles.map((profile, index) => (
            <details class="profile-card" open={index === 0}>
              <summary>
                <span class="profile-tag">
                  PROFILE // {profile.name.toUpperCase()}
                </span>
                <span class="profile-index">
                  P{String(index + 1).padStart(2, "0")}/
                  {String(profiles.length).padStart(2, "0")}
                </span>
              </summary>
              <table class="mapping-table profile-table">
                <thead>
                  <tr>
                    <th>GESTURE</th>
                    <th>MAIN / A</th>
                    <th>SIDE / B</th>
                  </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                  {gestures.map(([key, label]) => (
                    <tr>
                      <th>
                        {label}
                        {key === "long" && (
                          <small>
                            {release.config.gestures.long_press_ms} ms
                          </small>
                        )}
                      </th>
                      {(["main", "secondary"] as const).map((button) => {
                        const action = profile.buttons[button][key];
                        return (
                          <td>
                            <strong class="slot-label">
                              {actionLabel(action)}
                            </strong>
                            <small class="slot-detail">
                              {actionDetail(action)}
                            </small>
                          </td>
                        );
                      })}
                    </tr>
                  ))}
                </tbody>
              </table>
            </details>
          ))}
        </div>
      ) : (
        <p class="muted body-copy">
          Profile dossiers appear here when a firmware package is available.
        </p>
      )
    }
    <p class="micro-copy">
      Profiles belong to this firmware build. Unassigned holds act as taps;
      unassigned double taps send two taps.
    </p>
  </article>
  <article class="panel guide-panel">
    <div class="panel-heading">
      <h2>03 / PAIR & OPERATE</h2><span class="small-tag">BLE</span>
    </div>
    <ol class="steps">
      <li>
        <span
          >Power on the Stick-S3 and open your computer’s Bluetooth settings.</span>
      </li><li>
        <span
          >Pair with <strong
            >{
              release?.config.bluetooth.name ??
                "the Bluetooth name shown on the device"
            }</strong
          >. It appears as a keyboard.</span>
      </li><li>
        <span
          >Wait for <strong>SECURE</strong> on the screen. Focus the window that
          should receive input: terminal, editor, or chat.</span>
      </li><li>
        <span
          >Press <strong>A + B</strong> to switch profiles. <strong>B</strong> steps
          forward, <strong>A</strong> engages.</span>
      </li>
    </ol>
    <p class="micro-copy">
      Macros type into whatever has focus, so aim before you fire. Input while
      disconnected is discarded, so old presses never play back after
      reconnecting.
    </p>
  </article>
  <article class="panel guide-panel recovery-panel">
    <div class="panel-heading">
      <h2>04 / RECOVER THE SIGNAL</h2><span class="small-tag">HELP</span>
    </div>
    <details>
      <summary>Device doesn’t appear?</summary><p>
        Use a USB data cable, try another USB port, and close serial monitors or
        other tabs using the device. Select the Stick-S3 in the browser’s USB
        chooser.
      </p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Connection or installation failed?</summary><p>
        Reconnect USB. Hold the side reset button until the internal green LED
        flashes to enter download mode. The port may change; connect again and
        retry. <a href={product.hardwareGuide}
          >Official Stick-S3 recovery guide ↗</a>
      </p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Bluetooth won’t reconnect?</summary><p>
        Hold both application buttons during startup for three seconds and
        follow the on-screen progress to clear saved bonds. Forget the device in
        your computer’s Bluetooth settings, then pair again.
      </p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Upgraded from Deck Clicker? Keys act strange?</summary><p>
        The keyboard descriptor changed in the macro firmware. Forget the
        Stick-S3 in your computer’s Bluetooth settings, then pair it again so
        the host reads the new descriptor.
      </p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Need different macros?</summary><p>
        Profiles are compiled into the firmware. Edit the <code>profiles</code>
        in <code>config.yaml</code> and rebuild. This installer ships the
        configuration shown on this page. <a
          href={`${product.repository}#customize-with-yaml`}
          >Configuration instructions ↗</a>
      </p>
      <p class="warning-note">
        <strong>CLASSIFIED MATERIAL WARNING.</strong> The firmware manifest published
        by this site includes <code>config.yaml</code> in full. Never put passwords,
        tokens, or secrets in text macros.
      </p>
    </details>
  </article>
</section>
